
// Possible options ‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾\ {{{1

	What getters return when trying to reach non-existing element?

		- None				// this is what funcy getters usually do
		- Default (get_or)
		- Throw Error		// this is what py/hy getters usually do

	Variadic multi-val:

		- variadic:     f(x1, x2, ...)
		- non-variadic: f([x1, x2, ...])

	Arg order:
		
		// Clojure (and funcy) usually prioritizes for ->>

		1)	(clip x 0 3)	// good for: ->					(->  x (clip 0 3))
		2)	(clip 0 3 x)	// good for: ->>, partial		(->> x (clip 0 3))  (map (partial clip 0 3) xs)

		3)	(clip <x₁> :low 0 :high 3 <x₂>)		// good for: ->, ->>, partial	— downside is verbosity
			(f vrbl * optional_params)			// same

		// examples:
		((pflip div 3) 4)
		((partial oftypeQ int) "4")


// ____________________________________________________________________________/ }}}1
